From: ane-stack
Subject: [PATCH 0011] fuzz: fix silent no-op splice producing false UnexpectedAccepts

In gen_mutation's splice arm, `base.mil.replacen(from, to, 1)` is a silent
no-op when `from` is absent. The `ew_chain` generator uses inline fp16 list
consts with no `const()` wrapper, so a `const()→const(` splice produced an
*unchanged valid program*. The frontend correctly accepted it, and the run
misreported it as an UnexpectedAccept validation hole — inflating the laxity
count and masking real findings.

The splice now falls back to a guaranteed-hit keyword (`func main→frob`) when
the chosen target is absent. Adds two regression tests: every mutation must
change the text, and a const() splice on a constless base must not no-op.

Verified on h17 (500 cases, seed 31337): the 4 UnexpectedAccepts are now
uniformly the documented func-name laxity; the no-op artifact is gone.

Found by PROBE-1 (docs/spec/ane-frontend-h17.md).

Stacking: apply after 0001..0010.
